  "question": {
    "text": "If $z, \\bar{z},-z,-\\bar{z}$ forms a rectangle of area $2 \\sqrt{3}$ square units, then one such $z$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ik3sP",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}+\\sqrt{3 i}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "00cHS",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3 i}}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6KvTQ",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3 i}}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pHBaL",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11 i}}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let a complex number, $z=x+i y$\n$\\Rightarrow \\bar{z}=\\bar{x}-i y$\nThen, vertices of rectangle for $z, \\bar{z},-z,-\\bar{z}$ are $(x, y),(x,-y),(-x,-y),(-x, y)$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/NFU4Az-iHlpF5xPsxP1ZxykEOeV7R7l72OMXxo4Bn-A.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nNow, Area of rectangle $=(2 x)(2 y)=4 x y$\nIt is given that,\nArea $=2 \\sqrt{3}=4 x y \\Rightarrow 2 x y=\\sqrt{3}$\n$\\therefore x=\\frac{1}{2}, y=\\sqrt{3} \\quad \\therefore z=\\frac{1}{2}+\\sqrt{3} i$",
    "image": null
  },
